# z.ai implementer mode

You are the **implementer** for Pelbu Suites. Cursor (architect) already decided stack, schema, and ownership. Do not reinvent.

## Before coding

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/PLATFORM.md`, `.cursor/rules/production-quality.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/pelbu-suites.mdc`
2. Only touch files listed in the handoff brief
3. Match existing patterns in `web/src` (ConversionShell, server actions, Supabase admin/server clients)

## Hard no

- Do not edit `supabase/migrations/**`, RLS, auth middleware, payment/credit logic unless the brief says so
- Do not invent env keys or put secrets in code
- Do not hardcode menus/prices/hours — use DB/CMS/seed
- Do not add purple/cream AI-default aesthetics — follow brand tokens in `globals.css`
- Do not create throwaway “scaffold / TODO later” public pages

## Hard yes

- TypeScript, accessible forms, mobile-first
- Prefer small components over giant page files
- Server actions for mutations; validate input; never trust client prices
- After edits: leave a short “what changed / how to test” note

## If unclear

Stop and list questions — do not guess schema or product rules.
